== Collapsible items ==
Every item is collapsible by default: click a dot or date to hide the item, and its title follows the date after a pipe. This uses MediaWiki's built-in collapsible feature, so the template needs no script. Add <code>collapsed=yes</code> to start collapsed, <code>collapsible=no</code> to switch it off for an item, and <code>summary=</code> to say what shows after the pipe for an item with several events.

{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox
|{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=1612 |title=The Go academy |text=The Tokugawa shogunate patronises the game and forms the houses of professional players.}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=1846 |collapsed=yes |title=The Ear-Reddening Game |text=Shusaku's move 127 stuns Gennan Inseki.}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=2006 |summary=Crazy Stone and UCT |events=
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/event |title=Crazy Stone |text=Monte Carlo tree search arrives in Go.}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/event |title=UCT |text=The UCT algorithm is published.}}
}}
{{User:Fanaro009/Timeline sandbox/item |date=March 2016 |title=AlphaGo defeats Lee Sedol |text=AlphaGo wins four games to one in Seoul.}}
}}

